68
00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.979
Don't forget to take the quiz below.
I hope this was useful to you  

69
00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.715
and that you had fun too.

70
00:06:09.715 --> 00:06:14.643
There's lots more to learn so maybe you'll take an online class
or two.

71
00:06:14.643 --> 00:06:19.641
I'd be honored to have the opportunity to teach you.

72
00:06:19.641 --> 00:06:22.235
Many people with hearing loss do their best

73
00:06:22.235 --> 00:06:24.487
to avoid group listening situations,

74
00:06:24.488 --> 00:06:28.126
especially if there's going to be people that they're unfamiliar with.

75
00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:31.573
And I would count myself in that category.

76
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.440
Here's a photo of me in my 20s
at a family reunion. 

77
00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.300
Our family reunions were very noisy.
And this is my cousin. 

78
00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.699
And I remember this moment,
because I was totally faking it. 

79
00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.760
I couldn't hear most of what
he was saying 

80
00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:58.680
and I didn't tell him.
That was my go-to strategy—bluffing—at 

81
00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:02.400
that time. That was before I had
my cochlear implant. 

82
00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.580
In our group classes,
we talk about communication strategies, 

83
00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:14.220
and we discuss bluffing
because it is a communication strategy. 

84
00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.560
And we talk about the merits of it,
and some drawbacks. 

85
00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:24.480
And I find that it's an opportunity
to reflect a little bit more deeply, 

86
00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.740
even for my own learning.

87
00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:30.124
However in the hundreds of hours

88
00:07:30.124 --> 00:07:34.246
that I've spent teaching
people with hearing loss to read lips,

89
00:07:34.246 --> 00:07:38.040
there's one thing
that doesn't change from class to class.

90
00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.400
I'm always astounded by 

91
00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.340
the power of being with 
other people who understand

92
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.420
The power of being understood. 

93
00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.796
I invite you to try.

94
00:07:51.796 --> 00:07:55.557
That said, if a group class just is just not for you,

95
00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:58.839
I have suggestions for other ways to keep going.

96
00:07:58.839 --> 00:08:02.845
I've written them below. Check it out!

97
00:08:02.846 --> 00:08:07.406
As always, please like, subscribe, and share with others.

98
00:08:07.406 --> 00:08:09.480
Take care!